				I just want to say that this game is a lovely, meditative experience. The music is absolutely perfect for contemplation. The ASMR of the wheat crunching down and the gentle shushing of the death energy coming back to you is unparalleled. Even the insects are interesting to hear. Nothing felt auditorily grating. The visuals, although simple, worked phenomenally. I did have a few moments where the whole game froze, but they were very rare. I didn't get any eye strain and could notice the subtle environmental...			&lt;/div&gt;
